[lesson]   Solution: FIX_PLAN: Modify phases/quantize.py: (1) auto-promote model_free=True when model estimate > 70% of free VRAM AND scheme is weight-only (W4A16/W8A16/MXFP4/MXFP8/NVFP4) AND iters==0; (2) collapse the if model_free / else branches to ALWAYS use config-only detection (AutoConfig + is_moe_config + architectures[0]). This eliminates the full-model pre-load that OOMs AND avoids the MLLM AutoProcessor path that fails on this stripped Qwen3.5 model. AutoRound's ModelFreeCompressor then streams 12 shards at ~7GB peak VRAM, auto-detects Conv1d (linear_attn.conv1d.weight) layers as ignored, and packs remaining Linear layers into W4A16.;SMOKE_TEST: cd /root/_work/1/s/auto_quant && MODEL_ID='nightmedia/Qwen3.6-27B-Architect-Polaris2-Fable-B-F451' SCHEME=W4A16 ITERS=0 EXPORT_FORMAT=auto_round MODEL_FREE=true MODEL_FREE_FORCE=true QUANTIZED_MODEL_DIR=/tmp/smoke_quant timeout 600 bash phases/quantize_wrapper.sh;```;;
